{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan revised to fold in two levers discovered via instrumentation (d2df, linked discovered_from), grounded in docs/experiments/diag_runaway_matrix.py:\n- LEVER 1 (criteria-scaled primary step floor): replace the flat _VERIFY_MIN_STEPS=480 with verify_step_floor(c)=clamp(8c,48,480). Confirmed root cause: the flat floor hands an 8-criteria ticket ~10x the budget it needs; the surplus is spent wandering into the 77% re-read waste the runaway guard catches. Matrix: floor 50 -> 0/3 runaway (clean PASS ~100 calls); floor 240 -> 2/2; floor 480 -> 3/3. This makes typical tickets converge WITHOUT recovery; banking remains the net for genuinely large tickets. Pool arithmetic reworked as a function of c (f6fc c=8: N=32,pool=48,successor=16; clamp-max c>=60: N=240,pool=360,successor=120).\n- LEVER 2 (path-normalized read_file memo): the f6fc memo keys on exact (path,line_start,line_end) so re-reads at different ranges slip past (measured 48 reads / 11 distinct files, 77% re-read). Normalize read_file's memo key by path: cache whole-file content once, slice all ranges from cache. Adds agent_call.py to scope.\nScope +completion.py, +agent_call.py, +2 config keys (verify_steps_per_criterion=8, verify_step_floor_min=48). Next: plan-review."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786069440656919001,"uuid":"ce3e465a-8f2b-450e-990b-77693a6cf720"}